# Workflow Rule

- Source of truth order: `{{ manifesto_path }}` -> `ai.config.yaml` -> `.cursor/commands/*` -> `.cursor/rules/*` -> `Taskfile.yml`
- Generic execution gates live in `.cursor/rules/workflow-gates.mdc`.
- Stack-specific and repo-specific gates must layer on top through profile-specific rules instead of mutating the generic gate file.
- Use canonical tasks only:
  - `{{ task_command }} {{ task_build_name }}`
  - `{{ task_command }} {{ task_test_name }}`
  - `{{ task_command }} {{ task_lint_name }}`
  - `{{ task_command }} {{ task_verify_name }}`
  - `{{ task_command }} {{ task_review_name }}`
- Do not hardcode stack-specific commands in generic workflow prompts or hooks.
- For non-trivial work, planning and execution memory must live in explicit artifacts:
  - `PLAN::ISSUE-ID`
  - `PROGRESS::ISSUE-ID`
- Plan quality minimum:
  - `Execution Contract`
  - `Spec Coverage Matrix`
  - `Do Not Break`
  - `Acceptance Traceability`
  - `Open Questions / Blockers`
- Progress artifact minimum:
  - `Выполнено`
  - `Текущий шаг`
  - `Дальше`
  - `Spec Conformance`
  - `Решения по ходу`
